    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1407">

                <pb facs="0931" n="815" xml:id="pg815"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/277.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Special Agent Carothers.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 20, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>On behalf of Spanish cotton growers in Torreon district, from whom
                    Constitutionalists have seized large amount of cotton, Spanish Ambassador
                    requests aid of Department in arranging with Carranza for restoration of seized
                    property to owners upon payment by them by way of contribution of fifteen pesos
                    per bale of cotton.</p>
                <p>Bring matter to attention of Carranza and say that the Department considers that
                    it would be more advantageous in the long run to the Constitutionalist
                    authorities to enter into such arrangement than to continue to withhold from
                    these Spanish subjects the property in question, which latter course of action
                    would tend to place the Constitutionalist authorities in a bad light before the
                    governments of the world as oppressors of foreigners residing or having
                    interests within their jurisdiction. Urge acceptance of this arrangement.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
